    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Inherent risk is critical because an untrusted source (quicknotes_mcp's tool description) reaches an irreversible egress sink (add_note to a third-party hosted service) carrying restricted data (AWS credentials read from the user's home directory), with no step/runtime limit to cap the autonomy modifier. The only declared control, a first-call approval that is then remembered as 'always allow,' provides no residual credit under the remembered-approval rule, so residual equals inherent at critical. Three further property findings -- an unrestricted Slack posting destination, no attributable audit trail, and unpinned filesystem/Slack tool definitions -- each rate high and do not change under the triggers considered, so forecast remains critical, driven by the same uncredited approval control and the complete absence of structural containment, egress restriction, or logging anywhere in the design."
  },
